ut in triple form, B3/B4 are mid-game), and its low number and lack of presence in current active sequences reduce risk. Discarding B5 or T7 threatens feeding possible pungs or kongs in active sequences (e.g., someone may be building B4-B5-B6 or T6-T7-T8 variations). Additionally, my hand lacks honors and terminals, and I\u2019m likely aiming for a minimal-scoring win via patterns like All Chows (2 points) or Mixed Shifted Chows (6 points), but currently not close. Safety and tile efficiency come first.\n\nAnswer: Play B2"}
